## Summary

Changes made inside the disposable run root:

**`src/types.ts:4`** — Added `"storehouse"` to the `BuildingKind` union.

**`src/sim.ts`**
- Added `storehouse` cost to `BUILDING_COSTS`: `{ wood: 25, stone: 10 }`.
- Added a new `BUILDING_PREREQUISITES` map (`Record<BuildingKind, BuildingKind[]>`) so each building can declare prerequisites. The existing hut/farm/quarry have empty prerequisite arrays (no prerequisite), and `storehouse` requires `["hut"]`. This keeps prerequisite logic data-driven rather than hard-coded.
- Added `export function availableBuildings(settlement)` which returns every building kind that is both affordable (via `canAfford`) and allowed (all prerequisites present in `settlement.buildings`).

**`tests/sim.test.ts`** — Added a `availableBuildings` describe block covering: storehouse is hidden until a hut exists, offered once a hut is built, and dropped again when it becomes unaffordable.

Design note: I factored prerequisites into a separate `BUILDING_PREREQUISITES` map (mirroring the existing `BUILDING_COSTS` pattern) rather than inlining a special case in `availableBuildings`, so adding future prerequisites is a one-line data change. The function iterates `BUILDING_COSTS` keys, so it stays in sync automatically as new building kinds are added.

Verified: `npm run test` → 7 passed; `npm run typecheck` → clean.


